/*  Shorthands — `src/Interpreter/ShorthandExpansion.cs`.

    ★ `Define shorthand gate as (and-gate or or-gate).` makes `gate` another way to WRITE that
    union and nothing more. Before anything is gathered, each shorthand's type is put back wherever
    its name is written and the declarations come out, so what is checked afterwards is the program
    its author would have written by spelling the type out each time.

    ★ The same as writing it out, down to the shape: `(gate or wire)` is the flat union of all the
    members, and `(gate or void)` the union with a void case — folded only where a shorthand went in,
    so a type with none in it is handed on exactly as it was parsed.
*/

Pull a book on collections.
    /// The program with every shorthand put back and every shorthand declaration taken out.
    Bind node or failure to expand-shorthands, given (the node program):
        Define everything as cast every-statement-in on (program).
        Define type-names as a map from text to fact.
        For each statement in everything, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ObjectDefinition" or statement's kind is "InterfaceDefinition":
                In type-names, the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)) becomes true.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define declared as a map from text to node.
        Define order as a series of text.
        For each statement in everything, repeat:
            If statement's kind is "ShorthandDefinition":
                Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
                Define shown as cast display-name on (name).
                Define at-row as cast number-of on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
                Define first as the entry for name in declared.
                If first is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the shorthand '{shown}' is already defined on line {(cast field-of on (first, 3))'s word}", "",
                        at-row, "define the shorthand '{shown}' a second time",
                        "A shorthand stands for one type. Give the second one a different name.")).
                Done.
                If (the entry for name in type-names) is not void:
                    Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{shown}' is already the name of a type", "",
                        at-row, "define a shorthand called '{shown}'",
                        "A shorthand is another way to write a type, so it cannot share a name with one. Give it a different name.")).
                Done.
                In declared, the entry for name becomes statement.
                Insert name into order.
            Done.
        Done.
        If the size of declared is 0, return program.

        // Each shorthand's own type first, so one may be written with another.
        Define resolved as a map from text to node.
        For each name in order, repeat:
            Cast resolve-shorthand on (name, declared, resolved, a series of text) or pass the failure off.
        Done.

        // `a new gate` names an OBJECT to make, and a shorthand is not one.
        Cast refuse-making-shorthands on (program, declared) or pass the failure off.

        Define holder as cast listed.
        Cast holder's add on (program).
        Cast put-shorthands-back on (holder, resolved).
        Return item 1 of holder's children.
    Done.

    /// A shorthand's type with every shorthand inside it put back — refused when it comes back round to itself.
    Bind void or failure to resolve-shorthand, given (the text name, the map from text to node declared,
            the map from text to node resolved, the series of text trail):
        If (the entry for name in resolved) is not void, return.
        Define seen as false.
        For each step in trail, repeat:
            If step is name, the seen becomes true.
        Done.
        If seen:
            Define opener as the entry for item 1 of trail in declared but void is cast listed.
            Define first-shown as cast display-name on (item 1 of trail).
            Define ring as "".
            Define inside as false.
            For each step in trail, repeat:
                If step is name, the inside becomes true.
                If inside, the ring becomes ring joined to (cast display-name on (step)) joined to " → ".
            Done.
            The ring becomes ring joined to (cast display-name on (name)).
            Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("the shorthand '{first-shown}' stands for itself ({ring})", "",
                cast number-of on (cast field-of on (opener, 3)), "define '{first-shown}' in terms of itself",
                "A shorthand is only another way to write a type, so it has to come down to a type in the end. Write the type out in one of them.")).
        Done.
        Insert name into trail.
        Define declaration as the entry for name in declared but void is cast listed.
        For each inner in cast shorthands-written-in on (cast field-of on (declaration, 2), declared), repeat:
            Cast resolve-shorthand on (inner, declared, resolved, trail) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Remove item (the number of trail) from trail.
        Define holder as cast listed.
        Cast holder's add on (cast copied-node on (cast field-of on (declaration, 2))).
        Cast put-shorthands-back on (holder, resolved).
        In resolved, the entry for name becomes item 1 of holder's children.
    Done.

    /// The shorthands a type names, in the order it names them.
    Bind series of text to shorthands-written-in, given (the node shape, the map from text to node declared):
        Define found as a series of text.
        Cast gather-shorthands-written on (shape, declared, found).
        Return found.
    Done.

    Bind void to gather-shorthands-written, given (the node shape, the map from text to node declared,
            the series of text found):
        If shape's kind is "atom", return.
        If shape's kind is "ObjectType":
            If cast is-filled-type on (shape):
                Cast gather-shorthands-written on (cast field-of on (shape, 2), declared, found).
                Return.
            Done.
            Define name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)).
            If (the entry for name in declared) is not void, insert name into found.
            Return.
        Done.
        For each child in shape's children, repeat:
            Cast gather-shorthands-written on (child, declared, found).
        Done.
    Done.

    /// Every shorthand under `tree` replaced by a copy of its type, every declaration of one taken out,
    /// and every union or voidable a shorthand went into folded as the parser would have read it written
    /// out. Whether anything changed.
    Bind fact to put-shorthands-back, given (the node tree, the map from text to node resolved):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return false.
        Define changed as false.
        If tree's kind is "list":
            Define back as the number of tree's children.
            While back is greater than 0, repeat:
                If (item back of tree's children)'s kind is "ShorthandDefinition":
                    Remove item back from tree's children.
                    The changed becomes true.
                Done.
                Decrement back by 1.
            Done.
        Done.
        Define place as 0.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            Define replaced as cast shorthand-meant on (child, resolved).
            If replaced's kind is not "atom":
                Cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, cast copied-node on (replaced)).
                The changed becomes true.
            Done.
            Otherwise if cast put-shorthands-back on (child, resolved):
                The changed becomes true.
                If child's kind is "UnionType" or child's kind is "VoidableType":
                    Cast rewrite-field on (tree, place, cast folded-shape on (child)).
                Done.
            Done.
        Done.
        Return changed.
    Done.

    /// The type a shorthand stands for, when `shape` is one written bare — otherwise an atom.
    Bind node to shorthand-meant, given (the node shape, the map from text to node resolved):
        If shape's kind is not "ObjectType" or cast is-filled-type on (shape), return cast atom on ("_").
        Return the entry for cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (shape, 1)) in resolved but void is cast atom on ("_").
    Done.

    /// A union flattened and a voidable of a union made a union with a void case — the parser's reading.
    Bind node to folded-shape, given (the node shape):
        If shape's kind is "VoidableType":
            Define inner as cast field-of on (shape, 1).
            If inner's kind is "UnionType" or inner's kind is "VoidableType", the inner becomes cast folded-shape on (inner).
            If inner's kind is "UnionType" and cast is-open-union on (inner) is false:
                Define cases as cast listed.
                For each one-case in cast union-cases on (inner), repeat:
                    Cast cases's add on (one-case).
                Done.
                Cast cases's add on (cast plain-type on ("VoidType")).
                Return cast made on ("UnionType", a series with (cases)).
            Done.
            Return cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (inner)).
        Done.
        If shape's kind is not "UnionType" or cast is-open-union on (shape), return shape.
        Define flat as a series of node.
        For each written in cast union-cases on (shape), repeat:
            Define one-case as written.
            If written's kind is "UnionType" or written's kind is "VoidableType", the one-case becomes cast folded-shape on (written).
            If one-case's kind is "UnionType" and cast is-open-union on (one-case) is false:
                For each held in cast union-cases on (one-case), repeat:
                    Insert held into flat.
                Done.
            Done.
            Otherwise, insert one-case into flat.
        Done.
        // (T or void) is a voidable T, as the parser reads it.
        If the number of flat is 2:
            If (item 1 of flat)'s kind is "VoidType", return cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (item 2 of flat)).
            If (item 2 of flat)'s kind is "VoidType", return cast made on ("VoidableType", a series with (item 1 of flat)).
        Done.
        Define cases as cast listed.
        For each one-case in flat, repeat:
            Cast cases's add on (one-case).
        Done.
        Return cast made on ("UnionType", a series with (cases)).
    Done.

    /// `a new gate`, where `gate` is a shorthand — refused, as C# refuses it.
    Bind void or failure to refuse-making-shorthands, given (the node tree, the map from text to node declared):
        If tree's kind is "atom", return.
        If tree's kind is "ObjectLiteral":
            Define made-name as cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (tree, 1)).
            If (the entry for made-name in declared) is not void:
                Define shown as cast display-name on (made-name).
                Return a failure (cast refusal-of on ("'{shown}' is a shorthand for a type, not an object", "",
                    cast number-of on (cast field-of on (tree, 4)), "make a new '{shown}'",
                    "Only an object can be made. Make one of the types '{shown}' stands for.")).
            Done.
        Done.
        For each child in tree's children, repeat:
            Cast refuse-making-shorthands on (child, declared) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
    Done.
Done.
